"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":481,"renderedHeight":308,"naturalWidth":481,"naturalHeight":308,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 818 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":11118},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6001a1f2.gif","alt":"This figure is a bar graph that displays data from 48 reporting areas (excludes California, Florida, Maryland, and New Hampshire) for 2007 showing the abortion rate (i.e., the number of abortions per 1,000 women aged 15-44 years, the abortion ratio (i.e., the number of abortions per 1,000 live births), and the percentage of total abortions by the age group of women who obtained an abortion. Among the 48 areas that reported by age for 2007, women aged 20-29 years accounted for the majority (56.9%) of abortions and had the highest abortion rates (29.4 and 21.4 abortions per 1,000 women aged 20-24 and 25-29 years, respectively). Women in the youngest and oldest age groups (<15 or ≥40 years) accounted for the smallest percentage of abortions (0.5% and 3.2%, respectively) and had the lowest abortion rates (1.2 and 2.6 abortions per 1,000 women aged <15 and ≥40 years, respectively).","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":481,"renderedHeight":356,"naturalWidth":481,"naturalHeight":356,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 889 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":21414},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/s6001a1f3.gif","alt":"This figure is a bar graph that displays data for 40 reporting areas (excludes California, Connecticut, District of Columbia, Florida, Illinois, Louisiana, Maryland, Massachusetts, Nebraska, New Hampshire, Rhode Island, and Wisconsin) showing the percentage of women who obtained abortions at ≤8 weeks' gestation, 9-13 weeks' gestation, or >13 weeks' gestation. Whereas 44.4% of adolescents aged <15 years and 52.5% adolescents aged 15-19 years obtained an abortion by ≤8 weeks' gestation, 60.7%-70.9% of adult women aged ≥20 years obtained an abortion by this point in gestation . Conversely, 19.6% of adolescents aged <15 years and 12.1% of adolescents aged 15-19 years obtained an abortion after 13 weeks' gestation, whereas this percentage ranged from 6.7%-8.6% for adult women.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":481,"renderedHeight":313,"naturalWidth":481,"naturalHeight":313,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 782 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":23849},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_word.gif","alt":"Microsoft Word file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":1087},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_excel.gif","alt":"Microsoft Excel file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":644},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_ppt.gif","alt":"Microsoft PowerPoi